            <div xml:id="d810">

                <pb facs="0616" n="612" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg612"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.512/37: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-11T18:00:00-05:00">February 11, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Your 88, February 9, 4 p.m. It is the Department’s view that any special
                    taxes imposed exclusively for the support of the present hostilities in China
                    would clearly appear to be in effect “military exactions or contributions” from
                    which American nationals are exempt under Article I of the Treaty of Commerce
                    and Navigation.</p>
                <pb facs="0617" n="613" xml:id="pg613"/>
                <p>Should you have information showing that American citizens have been or may be
                    subjected to the special taxes in question, the pertinent facts should be
                    telegraphically reported together with your comments as to the advisability of
                    representations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
